  "description": "NVIDIA Nemotron Nano 12B V2 VL is a commercial-ready vision-language reasoning model for document intelligence, visual question answering, OCR-style extraction, image summarization, and multimodal chat. The upstream model card documents support for text, image, multi-image, and video inputs; this initial Forge profile exposes text plus image chat only, with video held back until Forge validates optional video request mapping and model latency. Forge reuses the official NVIDIA VLM NIM 1.5.0 container, mirrored by digest to all active Forge regional registries. Live Forge probes on 2026-05-30 support B200/us-central1, H200/eu-north2, L40S/eu-north1, and RTX6000/us-central1 with 10 measured image-chat requests per successful cell. B300/uk-south1 is disabled because the NIM vLLM BF16 profile selects SM103, then Triton rejects sm_103 during torch.compile and aborts before readiness. NIM cache data is written under /opt/nim/.cache, which Forge mounts from /mnt/data/forge-weights on model pods. Status remains onboarding and non-default until image-bound Triton r26.03+ evidence is attached for the exact NIM digest, B300 remains unsupported, and video input remains intentionally unexposed.",
